 R←Test_OnWait_004(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;expected
⍝ Exercise "SetOnWait": the function established is called once per question, with type and question
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 :If batchFlag
     R←T._NoBatchTest ⋄ →0
 :EndIf

 ∆OnWaitCalls←⍬
 ∆OnWaitSpy C.SetOnWait 0
 ∆Info'This test needs you: answer every question exactly as it tells you to'
 {}C.YesOrNo'TST1@Enter "x" first, then "y" - okay?'
 {}'TST2@Enter "9" first, then "1"'C.Select'First' 'Second'
 C.Pause'TST3@Just press <enter>'
 {}({(,'1')≡,⍵}C.AskForText)'TST4@Enter "x" first, then "1"'
 {}({1}C.AskForNumber)'TST5@Enter "a" first, then "1"'

 expected←⊂'YesOrNo' 'Enter "x" first, then "y" - okay?'
 expected,←⊂'Select' 'Enter "9" first, then "1"'
 expected,←⊂'Pause' 'Just press <enter>'
 expected,←⊂'AskForText' 'Enter "x" first, then "1"'
 expected,←⊂'AskForNumber' 'Enter "a" first, then "1"'
 →T.GoToTidyUp expected≢∆OnWaitCalls

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 C.UnsetOnWait
 ⎕EX'∆OnWaitCalls'
⍝Done
